 "apply_renames_note": "INERT. While false, collection_for() is the identity function and the physical collections keep their table names. Flipping this is a coordinated operation -- ship the resolver to BOTH repos, stop both containers, renameCollection the 13 that hold data, then flip and deploy both together. Flipping it in a plain deploy points live code at collections that do not exist, and Mongo creates them empty on first write rather than erroring.",
 "prefixes": {
  "log_": "append-only; never updated; read by time range",
  "state_": "mutable current state; one document per entity",
  "ts_": "time series keyed (entity, date)",
